Usage: slurm-notify --help | --version
       slurm-notify config validate --config <absolute-path>
       slurm-notify status --config <absolute-path>
       slurm-notify doctor --config <absolute-path>
       slurm-notify start --foreground --config <absolute-path>

Options:
  --help     Show this help
  --version  Show the package version
  --config   Explicit absolute configuration path
  --foreground  Run monitoring in the foreground

Commands:
  config validate  Validate configuration and local resources
  status           Inspect existing historical state
  doctor           Check local resources and bounded Slurm probes
  start            Run local foreground monitoring

Foreground monitoring accepts HTTPS webhook, SMTP and mixed routes.
Validate site polling/execution policy before monitoring a real cluster.
